# text = Twenty times a day why I do it a thousand times a day I wonder I wonder , looking back , to think how hopeful I was when the vessel sailed ; I never thought then of disappointment , but I pictured the joy of meeting , imagining the very words that would be said , the very tones , the very looks ; but for this last month of the voyage , day by day , and hour by hour my heart sinks and my hopeful fancies fade away , and I dread the end as much as if I knew that I was going to England to attend a funeral What a fool what a fool I am to be frightened at this ?
